      {
        "id": "U7-D6",
        "statement": "withdraw (V8) also checks InsufficientFunds against available instead of balance, still third, before DailyLimitExceeded. V3-R2\u0027s bullets name only debit and transfer, but its rule is \u0027money that is held cannot be spent\u0027, and a cash withdrawal spends money; V3 predates V8 in numbering and did not know withdraw existed. Leaving withdraw on balance would let held money be withdrawn. This departs from V8-R1 step 3\u0027s literal \u0027more than the balance\u0027 only when holds exist (a case V8 never considered); with no holds it is identical and every V8 test still passes. I resolved the same-level conflict in favour of the newer requirement\u0027s stated rule, per the directives\u0027 authority order; it is reversible by switching withdraw back to balance.",
